\title{Specifying the Machine: Sail, LLZK, zkLean}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The other half of a verified zkVM: a trustworthy specification of the machine being proved, and
    a way to reason about circuits written in the many DSLs that exist. [LC3 in Lean](dhsorens-0027)
    is the same problem at a scale small enough to see all of it.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The Sail Lean backend: extracting the RISC-V specification into Lean, and what fidelity
        that gives.}
        \li{LLZK as an MLIR dialect unifying circuits from different DSLs — what it can and cannot
        express.}
        \li{zkLean for [R1CS](dhsorens-002S), alongside [Clean](dhsorens-002Y) for
        [AIR](dhsorens-002U).}
        \li{The gap between an ISA specification and the constraint system claiming to implement
        it.}
        \li{Whether the EVM track's route (revm against KEVM, KEVM against a Lean model) is the
        right shape for the zkVM track too.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: [Verified-zkEVM overview](https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/Overview).
}
